      "question_text": "Argyll Robertson pupil: characteristics?",
      "options": {
        "A": "Reacts to light, not accommodation",
        "B": "Does not react to light but reacts to accommodation (near)",
        "C": "Both reactions absent",
        "D": "Both reactions present but sluggish"
      },
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Argyll Robertson pupil: accommodation-convergence reflex intact, but light reflex ABSENT (midbrain dorsal lesion). Classic in neurosyphilis. Bilateral, irregular, small (miotic) pupils."
    },
