      "question_text": "Bitemporal hemianopia indicates lesion at?",
      "options": {
        "A": "Optic nerve",
        "B": "Optic chiasm",
        "C": "Optic tract",
        "D": "Visual cortex"
      },
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Bitemporal hemianopia: chiasmal lesion (crossing nasal fibers). Pituitary adenoma most common cause. Optic nerve: monocular visual loss. Optic tract/radiation: homonymous hemianopia."
